From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the guest's scanout IOSurface as the layer's contents

What: a scanout buffer that virgl made as an IOSurface
(virgl-scanout-iosurface.patch) goes on the layer as it is: no draw into the
present's surfaces, which are then not made at all. It waits for the guest's GPU
work on it (virgl's fence after the last write, in the present queue) as a drawn
frame waits for its draw, takes the vsync queue like any frame, and is tagged with
the colour space a present surface would have (sRGB, or PQ for a 10-bit buffer with
HDR on; the layer then shows it with EDR). The buffer sent last, flushed again with
nothing written, is not sent again (a write moves it to another IOSurface): the
guest flushes most buffers twice.
Drawn instead, from the IOSurface as a RECTANGLE texture: a frame of extra
brightness (the brightness shader reading a RECTANGLE texture). Such a frame waits
for the guest's writes on the GPU and keeps the IOSurface in use until its draw is
done; if it cannot be drawn, the last good frame stays. A second output's window,
the CAOpenGLLayer path (GPU safe mode) and the boot logo's probe read the buffer's
RECTANGLE texture the same way, and keep the IOSurface in use until the GPU is done
with the draw; DisplayGLTexture carries the IOSurface and its fence operations
(virtio-gpu-virgl.c). The tiled present and the partial present's check
mode leave such buffers alone. qemu.log once a minute: "cocoa: the guest's IOSurface
frames, last minute: ...".
Test hook OMACVM_TEST_PACE_CHECK=1: as each whole frame goes on the layer, QEMU reads
its surface (plain surfaces only) and counts frames written while shown (a 16 x 16
grid of pixels changed after the frame went up); with tests/graphics/pacing's page
and a second counter strip at its bottom also torn frames, the counter's steps, and
the marker's flips for key latency.
Why: the present's draw cost 0.60 ms of GPU a frame at 5120x2880.
Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's IOSurface present).
Tests: VM A/B and the frame check in docs/experiments/display-path.md.
Applies before omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch (the last cocoa patch), with
virgl-scanout-iosurface.patch.
